dragon-drop (lightweight drag-and-drop source and target)

dragon-drop provides a small GTK+3 window for dragging files into apps
that expect file-manager style drag-and-drop. It can also act as a drop
target and print received files or text to standard output.

It is useful from scripts and shells on X or Wayland systems.

Upstream calls this program dragon. This SlackBuild installs it as
dragon-drop to avoid conflicting with Slackware's KDE Dragon Player
package.

Homepage: https://github.com/mwh/dragon
